  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "403f9fd6-565f-443d-9aeb-801ae066ad3c",
    "name": "Fortnox REST API (Representative Subset) Accounts Suppliers API",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": {
      "content": "Grounded OpenAPI description of the Fortnox REST API - the Swedish cloud accounting/ERP platform for SMBs and accounting bureaus. Base URL is https://api.fortnox.se/3/. Authentication is OAuth2 Authorization Code Flow: each request carries the Access-Token (Bearer JWT, 1h) header plus the Client-Secret header issued to your Fortnox app. The old fixed Access-Token/Client-Secret integration keys were deprecated 2025-04-30.\n\nSCOPE / FIDELITY NOTE: The Fortnox API exposes 40+ resources. This document ships a solid, representative SUBSET (Invoices, Customers, Articles, Orders, Offers, Vouchers, Accounts, Financial Years, Suppliers, Supplier Invoices, Projects) with pragmatic, partial field-level schemas. Paths, methods, identifiers, the wrapper-object response envelope (e.g. { \"Invoice\": {...} }, { \"Invoices\": [...] }), and auth are grounded in Fortnox's developer documentation. Per-field property coverage is intentionally partial and MODELED/summarized from the docs, not transcribed field-for-field for every resource. Verify exact field sets and validation against https://api.fortnox.se/apidocs before production use.\n\nContact Support:\n Name: Fortnox Developer",
      "type": "text/plain"
    }
  }
